{"actor":"literature","data":{"citation":{"first_author":"Muhammad Jauhar Vikri","identifier":"doi:10.64479/iarci.v1i2.61","title":"Impact of Data Normalization on K-Nearest Neighbor Classification Performance: A Case Study on Date Fruit Dataset","year":2026},"claim":"Z-score standardization leads to the highest and most consistent classification accuracy in KNN models compared to other normalization methods.","concepts":["feature scaling","standardization","nearest neighbor","accuracy"],"id":"E1","quote":"Z-score standardization achieves the highest and most stable accuracy, followed by Min–Max normalization.","stance":"supports"},"hash":"95e786f31228f734f7019347cbef21e08cc69d914873c1e29137402536bad2a1","kind":"artefact","prev":"da9b9781fe4d1cfee412d5087b3ab891e08ef82cfe4afd2ccb168eb4175de51c","seq":12,"stage":"evidence","ts":"2026-10-10T06:03:10.673+00:00"}
{"actor":"literature","data":{"citation":{"first_author":"Jonson Manurung","identifier":"doi:10.35335/mandiri.v14i2.466","title":"Optimizing the performance of the K-Nearest Neighbors algorithm using grid search and feature scaling to improve data classification accuracy","year":2025},"claim":"Applying feature scaling in combination with parameter optimization significantly improves KNN accuracy, achieving 97.19% compared to a baseline of 93.86%.","concepts":["feature scaling","standardization","nearest neighbor","accuracy"],"id":"E2","quote":"The optimized KNN configuration with k = 9, weights = distance, and metric = manhattan achieved an average accuracy of 97.19%, outperforming the baseline accuracy of 93.86%.","stance":"supports"},"hash":"a17d6e65e752c8f2c3033dce761d78ad920e222bd7e9891c3f900df81fcf9420","kind":"artefact","prev":"95e786f31228f734f7019347cbef21e08cc69d914873c1e29137402536bad2a1","seq":13,"stage":"evidence","ts":"2026-10-10T06:03:10.673+00:00"}
{"actor":"literature","data":{"citation":{"first_author":"Dadi Rahmat","identifier":"doi:10.1109/iceei52609.2021.9611110","title":"Heart Disease Prediction Using K-Nearest Neighbor","year":2021},"claim":"The study explicitly uses standardization of the dataset as part of its method to improve KNN performance in heart disease prediction.","concepts":["feature scaling","standardization","nearest neighbor","accuracy"],"id":"E3","quote":"The aim of this study is to improve the performance of heart disease prediction using standardization dataset and feature selection for KNN.","stance":"supports"},"hash":"970fb8fb1b6a344e458a1e9a87a5901a948331ca326db85c1f358e0044b5b1d3","kind":"artefact","prev":"a17d6e65e752c8f2c3033dce761d78ad920e222bd7e9891c3f900df81fcf9420","seq":14,"stage":"evidence","ts":"2026-10-10T06:03:10.673+00:00"}
{"actor":"literature","data":{"citation":{"first_author":"S. Basak","identifier":"doi:10.1109/smc42975.2020.9282834","title":"Evolutionary Feature Scaling in K-Nearest Neighbors Based on Label Dispersion Minimization","year":2020},"claim":"Feature scaling (via feature weighting based on dispersion measures) is used to improve KNN classification accuracy, with empirical evidence showing performance gains.","concepts":["feature scaling","standardization","nearest neighbor","accuracy"],"id":"E4","quote":"It is empirically demonstrated that these measures of dispersion can be indicative of the performance of KNN regression and classification. This idea is further used to learn feature weights that help improve the accuracy of KNN classification and regression.","stance":"supports"},"hash":"dd6c61d804bc59f9d3d4cf1dd6622e6562b19bee959b1a70692d8c8071b95537","kind":"artefact","prev":"970fb8fb1b6a344e458a1e9a87a5901a948331ca326db85c1f358e0044b5b1d3","seq":15,"stage":"evidence","ts":"2026-10-10T06:03:10.673+00:00"}
{"actor":"literature","data":{"citation":{"first_author":"Aria Aria","identifier":"doi:10.60005/coreid.v3i3.139","title":"Performance Comparison of K-Nearest Neighbor, Decision Tree, and Support Vector Machine Algorithms for Diabetes Classification","year":2025},"claim":"The study explicitly includes feature standardization as part of its preprocessing pipeline for KNN and other models.","concepts":["feature scaling","standardization","nearest neighbor","accuracy"],"id":"E5","quote":"The study aims to provide a fair and consistent comparison by applying unified preprocessing procedures, including median imputation for clinically invalid values, feature standardization, and stratified 5-fold cross-validation.","stance":"supports"},"hash":"ba5a161414d681a57cea4b4bbe402e6e2e2da631d9940b7cab5a7df2453951f9","kind":"artefact","prev":"dd6c61d804bc59f9d3d4cf1dd6622e6562b19bee959b1a70692d8c8071b95537","seq":16,"stage":"evidence","ts":"2026-10-10T06:03:10.673+00:00"}
{"actor":"literature","data":{"citation":{"first_author":"Tian Wang","identifier":"doi:10.1109/assp54407.2021.00044","title":"Time Series Classification Based on Multi-scale Dynamic Convolutional Features and Distance Features","year":2021},"claim":"This paper focuses on time series classification using convolutional features and distance features, but does not discuss feature scaling or its impact on KNN or accuracy.","concepts":["distance","accuracy"],"id":"E6","quote":"The main contribution of this paper includes three aspects: firstly, based on the multi-scale dynamic convolution operation, we propose a Multi-Scale Dynamic Convolution Network (MSDCNet). It uses multi-scale dynamic convolution to dynamically adjust the convolutional kernels for different input data and extract the features of time series.","stance":"context"},"hash":"71a178979e43cbaf67119733c5ecb3e00c6b410682ace6b8622aff0ef33223ec","kind":"artefact","prev":"ba5a161414d681a57cea4b4bbe402e6e2e2da631d9940b7cab5a7df2453951f9","seq":17,"stage":"evidence","ts":"2026-10-10T06:03:10.673+00:00"}
{"actor":"literature","data":{"citation":{"first_author":"Muasir Pagan","identifier":"doi:10.11591/csit.v4i2.p135-142","title":"Investigating the impact of data scaling on the performance of the k-nearest neighbor algorithm","year":2023},"claim":"Data scaling has a significant effect on the performance of the k-nearest neighbor (KNN) algorithm, meaning that how features are scaled can influence classification accuracy.","concepts":["feature scaling","standardization","nearest neighbor","accuracy"],"id":"E7","quote":"The results show that data scaling significantly affects the performance of the KNN algorithm, and the choice of scaling method can have significant implications for practical applications.","stance":"supports"},"hash":"6a0b8cf757a2bcf04fd00dff1864cb54f7f9fda6316ac57c8083baa94e31fd7d","kind":"artefact","prev":"71a178979e43cbaf67119733c5ecb3e00c6b410682ace6b8622aff0ef33223ec","seq":18,"stage":"evidence","ts":"2026-10-10T06:03:10.673+00:00"}
{"actor":"literature","data":{"citation":{"first_author":"J.K. Kanimozhi","identifier":"doi:10.1109/icctdc64446.2025.11158881","title":"Comparing SVM and KNN Algorithm for High Accuracy in Brain Tumor Prediction","year":2025},"claim":"In the context of brain tumor prediction, the KNN algorithm achieved higher accuracy than SVM, suggesting that KNN may perform well under certain conditions, though the study does not specifically evaluate feature scaling for KNN.","concepts":["nearest neighbor","accuracy"],"id":"E8","quote":"Group 1, which utilised the KNN algorithm, performed much better than Group 2, which utilized the SVM algorithm, with an accuracy of 94.56%.","stance":"context"},"hash":"0b41763174a46dce39c4fce7fe1b8cdc1ef4ac1ae8aa488ca3ec7400a2bdc8ac","kind":"artefact","prev":"6a0b8cf757a2bcf04fd00dff1864cb54f7f9fda6316ac57c8083baa94e31fd7d","seq":19,"stage":"evidence","ts":"2026-10-10T06:03:10.673+00:00"}
{"actor":"literature","data":{"citation":{"first_author":"Karaj Khosla","identifier":"doi:10.3390/a13080192","title":"Local-Topology-Based Scaling for Distance Preserving Dimension Reduction Method to Improve Classification of Biomedical Data-Sets","year":2020},"claim":"The method TPDS, which involves distance inflation to preserve local topology, improves classification performance in biomedical datasets by better preserving distance information and local structure.","concepts":["feature scaling","nearest neighbor","distance","accuracy"],"id":"E9","quote":"Applying TPDS on diverse biomedical data-sets revealed that besides providing better visualization than typical distance preserving methods, TPDS leads to better classification of data points in reduced dimension.","stance":"supports"},"hash":"362e85f482f02aa7afb1d25d3a9c25085005a5b7eb54b5b7cdf74f105f85349a","kind":"artefact","prev":"0b41763174a46dce39c4fce7fe1b8cdc1ef4ac1ae8aa488ca3ec7400a2bdc8ac","seq":20,"stage":"evidence","ts":"2026-10-10T06:03:10.673+00:00"}
{"actor":"literature","data":{"citation":{"first_author":"Chynthia Drinita","identifier":"doi:10.58477/cj.v4i2.512","title":"Comparison of Support Vector Machine and K-Nearest Neighbor Methods for Predicting Student Learning Outcomes Based on Student Performance Data","year":2026},"claim":"Feature standardization was applied as part of the preprocessing pipeline in a KNN model for student learning outcome prediction.","concepts":["feature scaling","nearest neighbor","accuracy"],"id":"E10","quote":"Feature standardization using StandardScaler, and data splitting into 80% training data and 20% testing data.","stance":"supports"},"hash":"b2fcbde09722cf997a14d048172e3005280d283344a96d071333077254fe15ba","kind":"artefact","prev":"362e85f482f02aa7afb1d25d3a9c25085005a5b7eb54b5b7cdf74f105f85349a","seq":21,"stage":"evidence","ts":"2026-10-10T06:03:10.674+00:00"}
